From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: athexweb3 <athexweb3@nirapod.org>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:46:26 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] armv8a: add the SHA-256 and SHA-512 instructions

SHA256H, SHA256H2, SHA256SU0, SHA256SU1, SHA512H, SHA512H2, SHA512SU0
and SHA512SU1 are added as intrinsics. They keep their assembly names,
without the V prefix, and their destination is also their first
source. Their semantics transcribe the pseudocode of DDI 0487 M.d (C7.2
and J1.4.3), reusing the SHA-256 functions of sha256.v, and they're all
data-independent-time (C5.2.4). A proof-only file outside the
extraction cone, armv8a_simd_lemmas.v, states in FIPS 180-4 terms what
the instruction descriptions compute: SHA256H and SHA256H2 do four
rounds, SHA512H and SHA512H2 with an element-wise add do two, and the
schedule pairs give the next message words. That fixes the role of
each operand. A test runs SHA-256 and SHA-512 of "abc" through the
compiler's semantics and checks the published digests, and the exec
test library is now a functor over the architecture for it.

FEAT_SHA256 and FEAT_SHA512 are optional and the compiler doesn't
check for them (#505), as with SHA-NI on x86. The printed assembly
doesn't enable the extensions either, so it has to be assembled with
them enabled. For the tests, scripts/check passes -mattr=+sha2,+sha3
to llvm-mc, as LLVM puts SHA-512 under sha3.

Co-authored-by: orvenweb3 <orvenweb3@gmail.com>
---
 compiler/scripts/check                        |   7 +
 compiler/tests/exec/dune                      |   3 +
 compiler/tests/exec/exec_armv8a.expected      |  12 +
 compiler/tests/exec/exec_armv8a.ml            |  24 ++
